{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793730572,"nonce":"NX8NTonalMa1Y1SBmmFt6Z7UYCM=","title":"An exception escaping a thread body aborts the process in the compiled tiers","message":"Thread.create(() -\u003e throw \"x\") ends the program in hybrid and jit with \"hlp_throw called without active trap; aborting\" (SIGABRT). Stock HashLink and the interpreter print the exception, end that thread and keep running.\n\nSeen from RayDE as ash.Future.then: the continuation runs on a Thread.create thread, so a throw in the success callback killed the page (\"thread N: unreachable\" on wasm32-wasip1-threads). Reproduced natively with a plain Thread.create, independent of ash.Future.\n\nCause: the fiber entry (std fiber::run_closure) calls the compiled closure with no trap armed, so Thread.create's rethrow finds none.\n\nFix: run every thread body under the host's setjmp boundary (hlp_set_trap_boundary, registered by the interpreter), print the uncaught exception and end the thread. Regression test crates/ash_cli/tests/thread_throw.rs covers interp, hybrid and jit at ASH_WORKERS=0 and 4.\n\nOpen:\n- wasm: not checked. Its trap is probably the same missing catch frame but the wasm runtime uses a different mechanism.\n- AOT binaries: thread bodies still run bare; not checked.\n- The compiled-tier message says \"instance of haxe.ValueException\" where stock prints the thrown value and stack.\n- ash.Future.then returns Void and runs continuations on a new thread; whether it should reject a derived future or marshal back to a caller's thread is a design question for ash-future.","files":null}]}